---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="InTellMe"
  description="Evidence-governed research, verification, and decision infrastructure. TruVector, ResearchOne, and the products they make possible."
  path="/"
>

  <!-- ── HERO ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-line">
    <picture>
      <source media="(max-width: 1023px)" srcset="/assets/imagery/hero-material-1400.webp" />
      <img class="hero__still" src="/assets/imagery/hero-material.webp" alt=""
           width="2400" height="1350" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
    </picture>
    <div class="hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="suite suite--flagship hero__inner">
      <h1 class="hero-line" id="hero-line">AI decisions should be traceable before they become consequential.</h1>
      <hr class="rule--champagne" />
      <p class="hero-support">InTellMe builds evidence-governed research, verification, and decision infrastructure for organizations operating in high-uncertainty environments.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#technology">Explore TruVector</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/investors">Investor Overview</a>
        <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.researchone.io/" rel="noopener">Try ResearchOne <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── TECHNOLOGY ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="technology" aria-labelledby="technology-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Core technology</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="technology-title">The work everything else rests on.</h2>

      <p class="lede reveal" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:66ch">Lane Vector is the research. TruVector is the product built on it. The
        method came out of chemical reaction kinetics, was first applied to
        search intent, and now governs how evidence is weighed before a system
        acts on it.</p>

      <div class="flagship" style="margin-top:48px">
        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <h3 class="product__mark--typeset" style="margin:0">Lane Vector</h3>
            <span class="badge">Research program</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">Kinematic modeling of intent and information dynamics.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:28px">Signals are treated as vector quantities with direction and rate of
            change, not as scalar counts. The approach is carried over from
            reaction kinetics, where a rate law is only valid for steps that are
            genuinely independent &mdash; the same constraint that stops one claim
            repeated five times from counting as five confirmations.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://www.lanevector.com" rel="noopener">Open Lane Vector</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <h3 class="product__mark--typeset" style="margin:0">TruVector</h3>
            <span class="badge">Validation and pilot development</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">Pre-execution arbitration of AI assertions before downstream systems act.</p>
          <ul class="states" aria-label="Decision states">
            <li>Allow</li><li>Review</li><li>Block</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top:28px">TruVector sits in front of consequential action. It weighs evidence, independence, and disagreement, then issues a decision a downstream system can obey.</p>
          <p>Lane Vector is the earlier modeling name for part of this work. The public product name is TruVector. Research notes live on lanevector.com and are subordinate to this page if they disagree.</p>
          <p>It does not rely on source reputation alone. It scores evidence quality, disagreement, and independence under an auditable policy.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://truvector.science" rel="noopener">Open TruVector</a>
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="/investors#request">Request the Technical Brief <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <svg class="product__mark" viewBox="0 0 240 240" role="img" aria-label="ResearchOne" style="height:34px;margin:0">
              <g transform="translate(120 120)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round">
                <polygon points="0,-110 95.3,-55 95.3,55 0,110 -95.3,55 -95.3,-55" stroke-width="7"></polygon>
                <path d="M -50,0 C -50,-40 50,-40 50,0 C 50,40 -50,40 -50,0" stroke-width="9"></path>
                <path d="M -40,12 C -40,-28 60,-28 60,12 C 60,52 -40,52 -40,12" stroke-width="9" opacity=".62"></path>
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3 class="room-title" style="font-size:1.5rem">ResearchOne</h3>
            <span class="badge">Private beta &mdash; early access available</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">Structured deep research that keeps sources, contradictions, reasoning lineage, and report contracts intact.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li>Sources stay attached.</li>
            <li>Contradictions are preserved.</li>
            <li>Reasoning lineage is kept.</li>
            <li>Reports obey a contract.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.researchone.io/" rel="noopener">Open ResearchOne <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="technology-strip reveal" aria-label="Technology illustrations">
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Illustration</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">An agent is about to file a record. The record waits until the evidence behind it is strong enough to allow, or thin enough to require review.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Illustration</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">A research report reaches two sources that conflict. The contradiction stays attached to the report instead of being averaged away.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Illustration</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">A news brief cites one wire story copied across outlets. The copies do not count as independent confirmation.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <!-- What is built, and what is not -->
      <div class="maturity reveal">
        <h3 class="room-title">What is built, and what is not.</h3>
        <p style="margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch">Each capability below carries its own state. Nothing is described as finished because the architecture calls for it, and the two unproven claims are named as unproven rather than buried.</p>

        <div class="maturity__grid">
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">Evidence object and decision path</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">The structured result a downstream system reads, and the Allow &middot; Review &middot; Block boundary it obeys. Schema and boundary are fixed and running.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--implemented">Implemented</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">Contradiction and divergence</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">Detecting that sources disagree, and carrying that disagreement into the decision instead of averaging it away. Detectable and measured; calibration is not settled.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--validating">Under validation</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">Independence-aware evidence</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">Discounting agreement between sources that share an origin, so that one claim repeated five times does not score as five confirmations.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--validating">Under validation</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">Quorum</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">The rule that decides how much independent agreement a claim needs before it may pass, given what acting on it would cost. Specified, not built.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--planned">Planned</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">AHE / HRA</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">Adjudication under conflicting evidence where no source is authoritative. Stated as a claim with a stated way to be wrong, and not yet demonstrated.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--hypothesis">Hypothesis</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="maturity__row">
            <span class="maturity__name">Kinematic validation</span>
            <span class="maturity__note">Treating a claim's movement through evidence over time as a signal in its own right. The most speculative element here, and the reason the research is research.</span>
            <span class="maturity__state"><span class="state state--hypothesis">Hypothesis</span></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="maturity__key">
          <div><b>Implemented</b> &mdash; runs, and measured</div>
          <div><b>Under validation</b> &mdash; protocol written, results partial</div>
          <div><b>Planned</b> &mdash; specified, not built</div>
          <div><b>Hypothesis</b> &mdash; a claim with a stated way to be wrong</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Where this sits against published work -->
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:64px;padding-top:48px;border-top:1px solid var(--bronze-edge)">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <h3 class="room-title">Where this sits against published work.</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:18px">Pre-execution gating for AI systems is an active area, and there is published work describing an Allow / Deny / Escalate decision in front of an agent's action. Two of those decisions look alike from the outside.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p><strong>They are not the same decision.</strong> The published approaches ask a permission question: is this actor allowed to take this action, under this policy? The answer is a lookup, and it is right or wrong.</p>
          <p>TruVector asks an evidentiary question: given conflicting sources of unequal independence, how well supported is the assertion this action rests on &mdash; and is that support enough for what the action would cost? The answer is a judgement under uncertainty, and it carries its own error bar.</p>
          <p>Policy gating and evidential adjudication compose. A system can want both, and neither substitutes for the other.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── PRODUCTS ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="products" aria-labelledby="products-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Commercial ventures</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="products-title">Products the infrastructure made possible.</h2>

      <div class="rooms">
        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/savr.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/savr.png 1x, /assets/logos/savr@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/savr@3x.png 3x"
               width="163" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">SAVR</h3>
            <span class="badge">Launching &mdash; web beta and Android testing</span>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">AI-assisted kitchen inventory and recipe planning that turns what you already have into meals.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://savr.cam" rel="noopener">Visit SAVR <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tools.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tools.png 1x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tools@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tools@3x.png 3x"
               width="107" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">Golden Goose Tools</h3>
            <span class="badge badge--live">Live</span>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">Instant technical SEO audit of a live page.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.goldengoosetools.com/" rel="noopener">Run an SEO Audit <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tees.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tees.png 1x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tees@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tees@3x.png 3x"
               width="84" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">Golden Goose Tees Studio</h3>
            <span class="badge">Storefront in beta</span>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">AI-assisted apparel design, with Printful-integrated placement, mockup, checkout, and fulfillment. The storefront is open on live payments; it has not been marketed and has not taken a first order.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.goldengoosetees.com/" rel="noopener">Open the storefront <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── RESEARCH ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Research</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="research-title">A public observatory.</h2>

      <div class="research__grid reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="pane__head">
            <img class="product__lockup product__lockup--sm" src="/assets/logos/waether.png"
                 srcset="/assets/logos/waether.png 1x, /assets/logos/waether@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/waether@3x.png 3x"
                 width="72" height="72" alt="" />
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">wAether</h3>
            <span class="badge badge--live">Live research product</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">Solar, galactic, and terrestrial telemetry from official government sources, each named on the page where it appears.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://www.waether.space" rel="noopener">Open wAether</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul class="sources" aria-label="Data sources">
            <li>NOAA SWPC</li><li>USGS</li><li>NASA DONKI</li><li>NOAA OVATION</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="caption" style="margin-top:24px">Pricing starts at $4.99/month or $49.99/year.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── COMPANY: current activity, research and validation ──── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="company" aria-labelledby="company-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Company</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="company-title">Built by Michael Brandon Lane.</h2>

      <div class="founder reveal">
        <p class="lede">InTellMe is an independent research and software company founded and operated by Michael Brandon Lane, a chemical engineer and chemist based in Johnson City, Tennessee.</p>

        <p>Before InTellMe, Lane worked at Celgard on lithium-ion battery separator and coating technology, including the development and scale-up of coated separator systems for high-volume manufacturing. He is a named inventor on multiple Celgard patents covering coated battery separators, including <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US11949124B2/en" rel="noopener">U.S. Patent 11,949,124</a>.</p>

        <p>That work shaped the standard he brings to software: evidence should be traceable, uncertainty should be explicit, and conclusions should change when the evidence does. Lane later moved from industrial engineering into independent software and computational research, applying the same measurement-first discipline to systems that evaluate information rather than materials.</p>

        <p>Today he designs and operates InTellMe and its products, including TruVector, which evaluates evidence, source independence, and disagreement before consequential decisions are passed downstream. InTellMe is self-funded and founder-run.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="rule" style="margin-top:56px" />
      <p class="kicker" style="margin-top:56px">Current activity</p>
      <h3 class="room-title reveal">Where each thing actually stands.</h3>

      <ul class="rail reveal">
        <li><span class="rail__name">TruVector</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">validation and pilot development.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">NSF SBIR Project Pitch</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">submitted December 2025, declined. A re-filing is planned.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">ResearchOne</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">private beta.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">SAVR</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">web beta and Android testing.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Tools</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">live and taking payment.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Tees Studio</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">storefront in beta; unmarketed, first order still ahead.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">wAether</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">live.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── FUNDING ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <!-- ── PROPERTIES: every live address, in one place ────────── -->
